rgia and Miami among the leading contenders for the five-star defensive end.","published":"2026-11-26T21:21:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50606035/sources-de-dj-jacobs-decommits-ohio-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Friday Night Lights,' 'Ted Lasso' top poll ranking 21st-century sports shows","description":"A Seton Hall poll crowns America's favorite modern fictional sports TV series.﻿","published":"2026-11-26T16:01:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/story/_/id/50576889/top-fictional-sports-series-21st-century","type":"Story","byline":"Brianna Williams","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"The oldest grudge in football","description":"When Texas Tech and its brash benefactor bought their way into the college football big time, they were settling an old West Texas score.","published":"2026-11-26T13:12:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50427039/texas-tech-puf-cody-campbell","type":"Story","byline":"Dave Wilson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Take a 360-degree look at college football's iconic rivalry trophies","description":"Whether ancient, animal or absurd, college football's rivalry trophies take many shapes.","published":"2026-11-26T13:09:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/feature/story/_/id/50371090/college-football-rivalry-trophies","type":"Eticket","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5146712/dylan-riley","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dylan_Riley_(American_football)"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Dylan Riley (American football)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dylan_Riley_(American_football)","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-25T17:07:11Z","intro":"Dylan Riley (born June 16, 2006) is an American college football running back for the Boise State Broncos.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Riley was rated as a three-star recruit and committed to play college football for the Boise State Broncos."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In week 3 of the 2024 season, Riley was named the Mountain West Conference freshman of the week after rushing for 96 yards and two touchdowns in a win against Portland State. He finished the 2024 season with 135 rushing yards and two touchdowns on 22 carries, while also returning a kickoff 96 yards for a touchdown. In week four of the 2025 season, Riley ran for 171 yards and four touchdowns on 19 carries, while also hauling in two passes for 84 yards and a touchdown in a victory over Air Force."}]}}